<urn:atm:triage:finding/AX4-QA-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AX4-QA-004" ;
  triage:title "Committed release-findings.json claims status fail / just lint failed while the live lint gate passes 35/35 at the same head" ;
  triage:description "AX.4 QA-1 (quality-mgr ax4-qa-r1, PR #1194 Final Quality Report 2026-09-05T09:14Z) at head aaf2e04bf. Commit aaf2e04bf 'chore(ax4): refresh validation findings' committed a regenerated scripts/validate_release.py artifact release-findings.json with status fail and a lint finding ('just lint failed', exit_code 1, blocks true, generatedAt 2026-09-05T07:22:40Z). quality-mgr and rust-qa-agent both re-ran python3 .just/run_lint.py all at this head and got 35/35 clean; rust-qa-agent full just validate regenerated the file with status pass. The committed artifact therefore misrepresents the run it claims to record (stale or dirty environment on the dev side). Not a gate failure, but a process-integrity defect. Fix: regenerate from a clean environment and commit an accurate artifact, or drop the artifact change from the branch; investigate why the original run reported a false lint failure." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-ax" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
